+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running go2rtc
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

go2rtc is configured in ${SYSCONFDIR}/go2rtc/go2rtc.yaml.  An example
configuration is installed there by the package.  It can be edited
directly or through the web interface at http://localhost:1984/.
The file is owned by the _go2rtc user so that the web interface can
update it.

Enable and start the service with:

	# rcctl enable go2rtc
	# rcctl start go2rtc

The daemon runs as the _go2rtc user.  By default it listens on:

	1984/tcp	HTTP API and web interface
	8554/tcp	RTSP
	8555/tcp	WebRTC (TCP and UDP)
	8443/tcp	SRTP (used by HomeKit)

These ports are reachable from the local network by default.  Restrict
them with pf(4) or change the "listen" options in the configuration file
if they should not be exposed.

The HTTP API can execute external programs through the echo, exec and
ffmpeg modules.  Do not expose it to untrusted networks without
additional authentication or a reverse proxy.

FFmpeg is not a hard dependency.  Install multimedia/ffmpeg to use
ffmpeg-based sources and on-the-fly transcoding.  Python 3 is required
for echo sources that use Python scripts.
